Motorola Mobility. ADSP GLINK Charger Specific Bindings

This glink charger driver is the target of redesign from qit_glink_charger
driver to make the glink charger driver more flexible, modularized
and compatible with old products using qit_glink_charger and new
QCOM platform products with complex charging HW design.

Glink Charger Driver Architecture:
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Userspace        batt_health/healthd/tcmd
-----------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Kernel                   glink_core                     (module main and provide common interface
                      /  |   |   |  \                    for glink devices, and common sysfs nodes
                     /   |   |   |   \                   like: adsp glink communication APIs)
                    /    |   |   |    \
                   /     |   |   |     \
                 batt   chg usb wls pump/buck/bcr       (glink devices response to handle it's own
                   |     |   |   |     |                 specific business)
                   |     |   |   |     |
-------------adsp OEM glink communication channel---------------------------------------------------------
                            |
                            |
           ADSP OEM GLINK MSG Receiver/Transmitter
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
glink_core.c
It's the main body of the adsp_glink_charger module to provide common
interfaces for all the registered glink devices, manage all the glink
devices and provide common sysfs nodes for functionality or debugging.

glink_batt.c
It's the glink device that handles all the battery related business
responses to get all batteries status information from ADSP and provides
optional battery supply and sysfs nodes for debugging or factory test.

glink_charger.c
It's the glink device that handles all the battery charging related
business, responses to get overall charger status information, connect
to mmi_charger driver for Motorola common charging policy controlling
and provides sysfs nodes for charging debugging or factory test.

glink_usb.c
It's the glink device that handles all the USB Type-C related business
responses for Motorola CID/LPD state handling and events broadcasting,
and support USB VBUS over temperature protection for specific SKUs.

glink_wls.c
It's the glink device that handles all the wireless RX/TX power related
business, responses to get wireless RX/TX information from ADSP, provide
sysfs nodes for Motorola specific wireless charging controlling, and
debugging or factory test.

glink_pump.c
It's the glink device that handles all switched charge pump related
business, responses to get charge pump information inside ADSP, and
provides sysfs nodes for charging specific debugging or factory test.

glink_buck.c
It's the glink device that handles all switched buck charger related
business, responses to get buck charger information inside ADSP, and
provides sysfs nodes for charging specific debugging or factory test.

glink_bcr.c
It's the glink device that handles all switched battery current regulator
related business, responses to get battery current regulator information
inside ADSP, and provides sysfs nodes for charging specific debugging or
factory test.

Benefit from glink charger driver design:
1. Easy upgrade, migration, and maintenance, as it's a common driver
   to be compatible with adsp based QCOM platform products.
2. Reduce develop workload, as developers can pay more energy and
   efforts on HW or platform specific business logic.
3. Easy to support complex battery charging solution, as it can support
   N couples of charger IC & battery pack in one system at the same time
   theoretically.

This glink charger driver is built as DLKM:
Module Name: adsp_glink_charger.ko
Log Tag: GLINK_CHG
Support Platform: adsp charging based QCOM platforms

devicetree properties description:
glink_common:
- type
 Usage:      mandatory
 Value Type: <u32>
 Definition: Set the glink device type to specify which kind of glink
device to be as.
bits[0:7]: glink device id: 0 ~ 0xFF to identify different sub-device
under the same device type specified in bit[8:15].
bits[8:15]: device type enumeration
GLINK_DEV_TYPE_BAT = 0,
GLINK_DEV_TYPE_CHG = 1,
GLINK_DEV_TYPE_USB = 2,
GLINK_DEV_TYPE_WLS = 3,
GLINK_DEV_TYPE_PUMP = 4,
GLINK_DEV_TYPE_BUCK = 5,
GLINK_DEV_TYPE_BCR = 6,

- polling-interval-ms
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: <u32>
 Definition: define the polling interval to notify glink devices to update status.

glink_batt:
- battid-utags
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: <string>
 Definition: battery id utags name

- df-serialnum
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: <string>
 Definition: default battery serial number

- profile-ids-map
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: Array of <string>
 Definition: Unlimited array of arrays. Each internal array needs to have a set
of 2 data members, each one representing this sequence: Battery Profile ID
(in integer value), Battery Serial Number(provided by battery spec). Battery
profile ID will be set to 0 if this property is not specified.

- battery-psy-enabled
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: <bool>
 Definition: decide if create a power supply for the battery

glink_charger:
- battery
 Usage:      mandatory
 Value Type: <dt-node>
 Definition: device tree node reference to battery bound to current charger

- mmi-charger-disabled
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: <bool>
 Definition: decide if register to mmi_charger driver for common charging policy controlling

- partner_psy_name
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: <string>
 Definition: decide the partner charger name used to sync partner battery charging state with charger in ADSP

- max-fcc-ma
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: <u32>
 Definition: Maximum fast charging current for configuring thermal charging mitigation

- thermal-primary-mitigation
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: Array of <u32>
 Definition: primary thermal mitigation table for battery charging mitigation.

- thermal-secondary-mitigation
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: Array of <u32>
 Definition: secondary thermal mitigation table for battery charging mitigation.

- encrypted-chg-enabled
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: <bool>
 Definition: decide if enable the encryption algorithm on charger identifiction.

glink_usb:
- therm-supported
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: <bool>
 Definition: decide if support usb thermal mitigation

- otp-en-gpio
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: <gpio node>
 Definition: gpio switch to control VBUS over temperature protection

glink_wls:

glink_pump:
- pump-psy-enabled
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: <bool>
 Definition: decide if create power supply for charge pump device

glink_buck:
- buck-psy-enabled
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: <bool>
 Definition: decide if create power supply for charge buck device

glink_bcr:
- bcr-psy-enabled
 Usage:      optional
 Value Type: <bool>
 Definition: decide if create power supply for charge bcr device

This glink charger was designed to be compatible with below HW/SW solutions:
Instance1: single battery charging in ADSP
ADSP pmic/wls/pump charging
+
AP mmi_charger + AP adsp_glink_charger
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Userspace  Common Interfaces for Charging Features and Factory Test
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Kernel           mmi_charger                            (Motorola demo, step, flash-fast charging,
                      |                                  factory and debugging interfaces)
                      |
              adsp_glink_charger                         (basic charging functions HW
                      |                                  specific factory debugging interfaces)
                      |
--------------------glink-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
                      |
                      |
                     ADSP
                  /   |    \
                 /    |     \
                /     |      \
               /      |       \
              /       |        \
            pmic   wls/pump   FG                        (Main battery FG and charging in ADSP side)

Velar Product Example:
adsp_glink_charger: mmi,qti-glink-charger {
	compatible = "mmi,adsp-glink-charger";
        def_batt: battery {
                type = <0x0000>;
                battid-utags = "mmi,battid";
                df-serialnum = "SB18D58448";
                profile-ids-map = "107000", "SB18D58448";
        };

        glink_charger {
                type = <0x0100>;
                battery = <&def_batt>;
        };

        usb {
                type = <0x0200>;
                therm-supported;
        };

        wireless_cps4035b {
                type = <0x0301>;
        };

        pump_charger_master {
                type = <0x0400>;
        };

        pump_charger_slave {
                type = <0x0401>;
        };
};

Instance2: dual battery charging in ADSP and AP
ADSP main battery charging with pmic/pump/buck/wls charger
+
AP flip battery charging with bcr charger and FG
+
AP mmi_charger + AP adsp_glink_charger
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Userspace  Common Interfaces for Charging Features and Factory Test
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Kernel               mmi_charger                            (Motorola demo, step, flash-fast charging,
                    /     |     \                           factory and debugging interfaces)
                   /      |      \
                  /       |       \
                 /        |        \
                /         |         \
               /          |          \
              /           |           \
             /            |            \
    adsp_glink_charger   bcr           FG2                  (basic charging functions HW
            |             |             |                    specific factory debugging interfaces)
            |             |             |                   (Flip battery FG and charging in AP side)
----------glink----------i2c-----------i2c--------------------------------------------------------------------------
            |             |             |
            |             |             |
            |          i2c chip      i2c chip
           ADSP
        /   |    \
       /    |     \
      /     |      \
     /      |       \
    /       |        \
 pmic wls/pump/buck FG1                                     (Main battery FG and charging in ADSP side)

Aura Product Example:
adsp_glink_charger: mmi,qti-glink-charger {
	compatible = "mmi,adsp-glink-charger";
        main_batt: main_battery {
                type = <0x0000>;
                battery-psy-enabled;
                battid-utags = "mmi,battid";
                df-serialnum = "SB18E07971";
                profile-ids-map = "107000", "SB18E07971";
        };

        glink_charger {
                type = <0x0100>;
                battery = <&main_batt>;
                partner_psy_name = "charger";
                max-fcc-ma = <5000>;
                thermal-primary-mitigation = <4000000 2900000 2000000 1000000 500000 300000 200000>;
                thermal-secondary-mitigation = <5000000 4000000 3000000 2000000 1100000 500000 100000>;
        };

        usb {
                type = <0x0200>;
                therm-supported;
                otp-en-gpio = <&tlmm 107 0>;
        };

        wireless_cps4035b {
                type = <0x0301>;
        };

        pump_charger {
                type = <0x0400>;
        };

        buck_charger {
                type = <0x0500>;
        };
};

Instance3: dual battery charging in ADSP
ADSP main/flip battery charging
+
AP mmi_charger + AP adsp_glink_charger
This solution supports battery property combination either in ADSP or AP.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Userspace  Common Interfaces for Charging Features and Factory Test
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Kernel           mmi_charger                            (Motorola demo, step, flash-fast charging,
                      |                                  factory and debugging interfaces)
                      |
              adsp_glink_charger                        (basic charging functions HW
                      |                                  specific factory debugging interfaces)
                      |
--------------------glink-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
                      |
                      |
                     ADSP
                 /    |      \
                /     |       \
               /      |        \
              /       |         \
             /        |          \
         pmic  wls/pump/buck/bcr FG1/FG2                (Main and Flip battery FG and charging in ADSP side)


Orion Product Example: battery status combination in ADSP side
adsp_glink_charger: mmi,qti-glink-charger {
	compatible = "mmi,adsp-glink-charger";
        def_batt: battery {
                type = <0x0000>;
                battid-utags = "mmi,battid";
                df-serialnum = "SB18E07971";
                profile-ids-map = "107000", "SB18E07971";
        };

        main_batt: main_battery {
                type = <0x0001>;
                battery-psy-enabled;
                battid-utags = "mmi,battid";
                df-serialnum = "SB18E07971";
                profile-ids-map = "107000", "SB18E07971";
        };

        flip_batt: flip_battery {
                type = <0x0002>;
                battery-psy-enabled;
                battid-utags = "mmi,battid-1";
                df-serialnum = "SB18E07970";
                profile-ids-map = "107000", "SB18E07970";
        };

        glink_charger {
                type = <0x0100>;
                battery = <&def_batt>;
                max-fcc-ma = <5000>;
                thermal-primary-mitigation = <4000000 2900000 2000000 1000000 500000 300000 200000>;
                thermal-secondary-mitigation = <5000000 4000000 3000000 2000000 1100000 500000 100000>;
        };

        usb {
                type = <0x0200>;
                therm-supported;
                otp-en-gpio = <&tlmm 107 0>;
        };

        wireless_cps4035b {
                type = <0x0301>;
        };

        pump_charger_master {
                type = <0x0400>;
        };

        pump_charger_slave {
                type = <0x0401>;
        };

        buck_charger {
                type = <0x0500>;
        };

        bcr_charger_master {
                type = <0x0600>;
        };

        bcr_charger_slave {
                type = <0x0601>;
        };
};

Orion Product Example: battery status combination in HLOS side
adsp_glink_charger: mmi,qti-glink-charger {
	compatible = "mmi,adsp-glink-charger";
        main_batt: main_battery {
                type = <0x0001>;
                battery-psy-enabled;
                battid-utags = "mmi,battid";
                df-serialnum = "SB18E07971";
                profile-ids-map = "107000", "SB18E07971";
        };

        flip_batt: flip_battery {
                type = <0x0002>;
                battery-psy-enabled;
                battid-utags = "mmi,battid-1";
                df-serialnum = "SB18E07970";
                profile-ids-map = "107000", "SB18E07970";
        };

        charger_main {
                type = <0x0100>;
                battery = <&main_batt>;
                max-fcc-ma = <5000>;
                thermal-primary-mitigation = <4000000 2900000 2000000 1000000 500000 300000 200000>;
                thermal-secondary-mitigation = <5000000 4000000 3000000 2000000 1100000 500000 100000>;
        };

        charger_flip {
                type = <0x0101>;
                battery = <&flip_batt>;
        };

        usb {
                type = <0x0200>;
                therm-supported;
                otp-en-gpio = <&tlmm 107 0>;
        };

        wireless_cps4035b {
                type = <0x0301>;
        };

        pump_charger_master {
                type = <0x0400>;
        };

        pump_charger_slave {
                type = <0x0401>;
        };

        buck_charger {
                type = <0x0500>;
        };

        bcr_charger_master {
                type = <0x0600>;
        };

        bcr_charger_slave {
                type = <0x0601>;
        };
};

